@ 16.1.5 - Proto-Tabla-Sentani to Tabla
# citation: Pogostick Man, from Gregerson, Kenneth, and Margaret Hartzler (1987), “Towards a Reconstruction of Proto-Tabla-Sentani Phonology”. Oceanic Linguistics, Vol. 26, No. 1/2 (Summer – Winter, 1987), 1 – 29. Some allophony triggered where p~ɸ, and probably some others Some vowel assimilations, mostly dealing with central vowels
	d > r / medially
	N > ŋ / _#
	i > ∅ / V_ (with a few exceptions)
	e > ə / unstressed (possibly only in disyllables?)
	oi > oe
	o > e (sporadic, highly unusual)